 ## Overview
-Limited Secondary Ray Sampling is an optimization strategy for computing volumetric self-shadowing in distance-field ray marching. It reduces computational cost by limiting the maximum travel distance of secondary rays and adaptively reducing sample counts based on primary ray depth and local density [S1, unofficial]. Unlike global shadowing methods, it restricts self-shadowing to a local neighborhood, trading long-range accuracy for performance [S1, unofficial][S2].
